        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Ingress does not enforce TLS</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Ingress shop/storefront-ingress accepts traffic without TLS. Credentials, session cookies, and response data cross the public internet in cleartext, and there is nothing to stop an on-path attacker rewriting responses to serve malicious JavaScript.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:63
spec.tls is absent

Risk 25/25 (likelihood 5 x impact 5). Exposure: 1 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 7.

Remediation: Add a TLS block and force HTTPS redirection.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
