          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Secret shop/shop-db contains inline `data`/`stringData` in a manifest tracked in version control. base64 is an encoding, not encryption. Anyone with repository read access -- including every CI job, every fork, and the full git history after the value is &quot;removed&quot; -- has these credentials. Rotation is the only remedy once this has been pushed.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:80
inline keys: password, username

Risk 20/25 (likelihood 4 x impact 5). Exposure: 4 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Rotate the credential, then source it from a secret manager.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
