        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container can escalate privileges</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Elevation of Privilege</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>allowPrivilegeEscalation is not set to false on Container shop/postgres. A setuid binary or a `sudo`-like helper inside the image can gain more privileges than its parent process, which turns a limited RCE into root inside the container and shortens the path to a container escape.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:115
allowPrivilegeEscalation is unset or true

Risk 20/25 (likelihood 4 x impact 5). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 6.

Remediation: Set allowPrivilegeEscalation to false.</a:Value>
