        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>LoadBalancer Service has no source IP restriction</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Service shop/storefront provisions a cloud load balancer with no loadBalancerSourceRanges, so it is reachable from the entire internet. This bypasses the ingress controller and therefore also bypasses any WAF, authentication, or rate limiting configured there.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:51
type = LoadBalancer with no loadBalancerSourceRanges

Risk 20/25 (likelihood 5 x impact 4). Exposure: 1 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 6.

Remediation: Restrict source ranges, or move the workload behind the ingress controller.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
