        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>ClusterRole grants full cluster administration</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Elevation of Privilege</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>ClusterRole shop-operator grants `*` verbs on `*` resources cluster-wide. Any subject bound to it owns the cluster: it can read every Secret in every namespace, create privileged pods on any node, and modify admission webhooks to make the compromise persistent and invisible.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:156
verbs include &#39;*&#39;

Risk 20/25 (likelihood 4 x impact 5). Exposure: 4 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Replace the wildcard role with an explicitly enumerated least-privilege role.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
