    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-EB27941387</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>36</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>f3553f56-10e4-542f-8249-2fb0ffae220c</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Workload has no egress NetworkPolicy</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>StatefulSet shop/postgres has unrestricted egress. That is the exfiltration path and the command-and-control path: a compromised pod can reach any external host, any internal service, and the cloud metadata endpoint at 169.254.169.254 to steal node IAM credentials.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:99
no NetworkPolicy restricts egress

Risk 12/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 4). Exposure: 2 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 6.

Remediation: Default-deny egress; allow DNS plus the specific destinations required.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>f3553f56-10e4-542f-8249-2fb0ffae220c</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
