        <b:TargetGuid>f3553f56-10e4-542f-8249-2fb0ffae220c</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Workload has no egress NetworkPolicy</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-NET-002</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-406F7EE57C</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>37</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Internet-facing Ingress has no authentication or rate limiting</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Ingress shop/storefront-ingress is exposed to the internet with no ingress-level authentication and no rate limit. Whether that is acceptable depends on whether the backend authenticates -- but the absence of a rate limit is unconditionally a denial of service and credential-stuffing exposure.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:63
no auth-* annotations

Risk 12/25 (likelihood 4 x impact 3). Exposure: 1 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 7.

Remediation: Add rate limiting at the ingress; add edge authentication for non-public endpoints.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-NET-005</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Internet-facing Ingress has no authentication or rate limiting</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-NET-005</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-71337D0457</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>38</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>High</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Ingress uses a wildcard host</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>A wildcard host binds this backend to every subdomain, which enables subdomain takeover chains and makes cookie scoping decisions unsafe -- a cookie set on *.example.com is readable by every other service under it.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:63
hosts = *.shop.example.com

Risk 12/25 (likelihood 4 x impact 3). Exposure: 1 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 7.

Remediation: List explicit hostnames.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>High</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-NET-006</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>cabdc8c4-3b0e-5365-b233-5d210db6dc45</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Ingress uses a wildcard host</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-NET-006</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-462B615D86</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
