        <b:TargetGuid>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Container root filesystem is writable</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-010</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-D21F940692</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>47</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>750e221b-c157-551f-94be-601b211b7721</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container root filesystem is writable</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>A writable root filesystem lets an attacker with code execution drop a web shell, overwrite application binaries, or install persistence that survives a process restart. It also removes a cheap tripwire: with a read-only root, most post-exploitation tooling fails immediately and noisily.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:41
readOnlyRootFilesystem is not true

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Make the root filesystem read-only and mount emptyDir for writable paths.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>750e221b-c157-551f-94be-601b211b7721</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-010</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>750e221b-c157-551f-94be-601b211b7721</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Container root filesystem is writable</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-010</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-B4758BF8C0</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>48</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container image uses a mutable tag</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container shop/web references image `shop/storefront:latest` by a mutable tag. What runs in production is therefore whatever the registry served at pull time. This breaks reproducibility, defeats admission-time image scanning, and makes supply chain tampering hard to detect -- an attacker who can push to the registry can replace the image without any manifest change.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:23
image = shop/storefront:latest

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Pin images by digest.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-011</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Container image uses a mutable tag</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-011</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-DA9D637EFF</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
