        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-014</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-A03BACF399</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>53</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Workload uses the default service account</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Elevation of Privilege</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Deployment shop/storefront runs as the namespace `default` service account with its token automounted. The default SA is shared by every workload in the namespace, so any permission granted to it is granted to all of them, and token theft cannot be attributed to a specific workload.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:7
serviceAccountName is &#39;default&#39;

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 2 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Create a dedicated ServiceAccount per workload; disable automount if the API is not used.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-016</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Workload uses the default service account</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-016</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-A34C7C1078</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>54</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container binds a host port</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container shop/web binds host port(s) 8080. The service is reachable on every node IP, bypassing Service-level controls and NetworkPolicy, and it constrains scheduling in ways that make node-level firewalling brittle.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:23
hostPort = 8080

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Expose through a Service and an Ingress instead of a host port.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-018</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>32bdd750-ec7f-582c-8f04-72c91da0bfc2</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Container binds a host port</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-018</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-94801B75BC</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>55</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Workload has no egress NetworkPolicy</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Deployment shop/storefront has unrestricted egress. That is the exfiltration path and the command-and-control path: a compromised pod can reach any external host, any internal service, and the cloud metadata endpoint at 169.254.169.254 to steal node IAM credentials.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:7
no NetworkPolicy restricts egress

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 2 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Default-deny egress; allow DNS plus the specific destinations required.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-NET-002</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Workload has no egress NetworkPolicy</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-NET-002</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-7940C9851E</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
        <b:FlowGuid i:nil="true"/>
        <b:Id>56</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>cbb38ff7-c4bf-5dc7-85d1-410422749470</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Service account token automounted on the default service account</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Elevation of Privilege</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>The `default` ServiceAccount in namespace shop automounts its token into every pod that does not specify another SA. This is the most commonly abused foothold for lateral movement inside a namespace.

Evidence: &lt;implicit&gt;
automountServiceAccountToken is not false

Risk 9/25 (likelihood 3 x impact 3). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Disable automount on the default service account.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Medium</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>cbb38ff7-c4bf-5dc7-85d1-410422749470</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-RBAC-007</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>cbb38ff7-c4bf-5dc7-85d1-410422749470</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Service account token automounted on the default service account</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-RBAC-007</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-BD31E364C4</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
