        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Data store has encryption at rest disabled</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Information Disclosure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>aws_db_instance shop stores data unencrypted at rest. Snapshot sharing, disk decommissioning, and support access all become disclosure paths, and most compliance regimes treat this as a reportable control failure on its own.

Evidence: tf/main.tf:5
encryption is explicitly disabled

Risk 8/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 4). Exposure: unreachable from an external entity. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Enable encryption with a customer-managed KMS key.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
