        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Compose service uses host networking</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Spoofing</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>network_mode host removes network namespace isolation: the container can bind any host port and sniff all host traffic.

Evidence: docker-compose.yml:11
network_mode: host

Risk 8/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 4). Exposure: unreachable from an external entity. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Use a user-defined bridge network and publish only required ports.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
