        <b:Id>61</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>f7981437-198e-5e3b-8dd4-ea64abf6ab07</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container image is not pinned by digest</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Container shop/postgres uses a version tag rather than a digest. Version tags are still mutable in most registries, so this is weaker than it looks, though far better than :latest.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:115
image = postgres:15

Risk 6/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 3). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 6.

Remediation: Resolve the tag to a digest in CI and commit the digest.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
