        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Medium</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Single-replica workload is a single point of failure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Denial of Service</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>StatefulSet shop/postgres is internet-reachable but runs a single replica, so any crash, eviction, or node drain takes the service down. It also means a single successful resource-exhaustion request has full impact.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:99
spec.replicas = 1

Risk 6/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 3). Exposure: 2 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 6.

Remediation: Run at least two replicas with a PodDisruptionBudget and anti-affinity.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
