          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Remote content fetched with ADD</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Tampering</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>ADD with a URL downloads and unpacks remote content with no integrity check. If the upstream host is compromised or DNS is hijacked, arbitrary content lands in the image at build time -- a textbook supply chain injection point.

Evidence: Dockerfile:4
ADD from a remote URL

Risk 4/25 (likelihood 1 x impact 4). Exposure: unreachable from an external entity. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Download explicitly and verify a checksum or signature.</a:Value>
