        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Workload has no liveness or readiness probe</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Denial of Service</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Without probes, Kubernetes cannot tell a hung process from a healthy one. A deadlocked or resource-starved container keeps receiving traffic, which turns a partial failure into a user-visible outage and masks the early signal of an ongoing resource-exhaustion attack.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:41
no livenessProbe

Risk 4/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 2). Exposure: 3 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Add liveness and readiness probes.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Low</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>750e221b-c157-551f-94be-601b211b7721</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-019</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>750e221b-c157-551f-94be-601b211b7721</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Workload has no liveness or readiness probe</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-019</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
    <a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
      <a:Key>TF-6A7C7B9BFC</a:Key>
      <a:Value xmlns:b="http://schemas.datacontract.org/2004/07/ThreatModeling.KnowledgeBase">
        <b:ChangedBy i:nil="true"/>
        <b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>53412b27-c301-5c73-9dcd-cecf78da5cd3</b:DrawingSurfaceGuid>
