        <b:Id>68</b:Id>
        <b:InteractionKey>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:InteractionKey>
        <b:ModifiedAt>0001-01-01T00:00:00</b:ModifiedAt>
        <b:Priority>Low</b:Priority>
        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Single-replica workload is a single point of failure</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Denial of Service</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Deployment shop/storefront is internet-reachable but runs a single replica, so any crash, eviction, or node drain takes the service down. It also means a single successful resource-exhaustion request has full impact.

Evidence: k8s/app.yaml:7
spec.replicas = 1

Risk 4/25 (likelihood 2 x impact 2). Exposure: 2 hop(s) from the internet. Blast radius 5.

Remediation: Run at least two replicas with a PodDisruptionBudget and anti-affinity.</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Priority</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Low</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
        </b:Properties>
        <b:SourceGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:SourceGuid>
        <b:State>NotStarted</b:State>
        <b:StateInformation>TF-K8S-020</b:StateInformation>
        <b:TargetGuid>b5009d2d-68ab-53d1-bcd7-6bbaad1b988b</b:TargetGuid>
        <b:Title>Single-replica workload is a single point of failure</b:Title>
        <b:TypeId>TF-K8S-020</b:TypeId>
        <b:Upgraded>false</b:Upgraded>
      </a:Value>
    </a:KeyValueOfstringThreatpc_P0_PhOB>
