        <b:Properties>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>Title</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Database deletion protection and final snapshot are both disabled</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatCategory</a:Key>
            <a:Value>Denial of Service</a:Value>
          </a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
          <a:KeyValueOfstringstring>
            <a:Key>UserThreatDescription</a:Key>
            <a:Value>aws_db_instance shop can be destroyed with no snapshot retained. A compromised CI credential, or a plain mistake in a `terraform apply`, results in unrecoverable data loss -- this is the destructive end of the availability spectrum.

Evidence: tf/main.tf:5
skip_final_snapshot = true and deletion_protection = false

Risk 3/25 (likelihood 1 x impact 3). Exposure: unreachable from an external entity. Blast radius 0.

Remediation: Enable deletion protection and keep final snapshots.</a:Value>
